<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thebaid</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thebaid was the southern region of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, stretching from about Abydos to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-cataract">First Cataract</a> at Aswan. Under Roman rule it was an administrative district, the scene of a revolt against Roman taxation soon after the conquest, and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a>'s time a separate province. It is also known as a cradle of Christian monasticism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thebaid.jpg" alt="Thebaid" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dioecesis_Aegypti_400_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
